note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note Contract section 4 lines 114-116: the div on line 10 is copied 3 times by unroll; each copy is a
note run-time trap site (divisor a) recorded as omc-site 1 line=10 iter=k. The contract alone does not fix the
note numbering; erratum E7 does: 0-based counter values in emission order, so exactly iter=0, 1, 2
note (exp/diag-site-unroll.err). Same artifact as diag-site-unroll-plain.om.
om2 diag
fn f a ulong to ulong
s = ulong 0
for i ulong 3 unroll
s = add s div i a
end
ret s
end
